---

<Layout
	title="Trisection & Solved NCERT Problems | Coordinate Geometry | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn trisection of a line segment, centroid of a triangle, and solve exam-focused NCERT practice questions for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/coordinate-geometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Coordinate Geometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Trisection & Solved <span>NCERT Problems</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master finding points of trisection of a line segment, centroid of a triangle, and solving exam-focused NCERT questions.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · TRISECTION OF A LINE SEGMENT -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · TRISECTION</div>
					<h2>Points of Trisection</h2>
					<p>
						Points <strong>P</strong> and <strong>Q</strong> are said to <strong>trisect</strong> line segment <em>AB</em> if they divide <em>AB</em> into three equal parts (AP = PQ = QB).
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>Point P divides AB in the ratio 1 : 2</strong>
						<strong>Point Q divides AB in the ratio 2 : 1</strong>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Centroid of a Triangle</strong>
							<p>
								The <strong>centroid G</strong> of a triangle with vertices <em>A(x₁, y₁)</em>, <em>B(x₂, y₂)</em>, and <em>C(x₃, y₃)</em> is:
								<br/>
								<strong>G = ( (x₁ + x₂ + x₃) / 3, (y₁ + y₂ + y₃) / 3 )</strong>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the coordinates of the points of trisection of line segment joining A(2, -2) and B(-7, 4)</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Find P (divides AB in ratio 1 : 2)</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x = (1(-7) + 2(2)) / (1 + 2) = (-7 + 4) / 3 = -3/3 = <strong>-1</strong><br/>
								y = (1(4) + 2(-2)) / (1 + 2) = (4 - 4) / 3 = 0/3 = <strong>0</strong><br/>
								<strong>P = (-1, 0)</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Step 2: Find Q (divides AB in ratio 2 : 1)</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x = (2(-7) + 1(2)) / (2 + 1) = (-14 + 2) / 3 = -12/3 = <strong>-4</strong><br/>
								y = (2(4) + 1(-2)) / (2 + 1) = (8 - 2) / 3 = 6/3 = <strong>2</strong><br/>
								<strong>Q = (-4, 2)</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">The points of trisection are <strong>P(-1, 0)</strong> and <strong>Q(-4, 2)</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>If (1, 2), (4, y), (x, 6) and (3, 5) are vertices of a parallelogram taken in order, find x and y</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>In a parallelogram, <strong>diagonals bisect each other</strong> (their mid-points are identical!).</p>
							<p>Mid-point of AC = Mid-point of BD:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								( (1 + x)/2, (2 + 6)/2 ) = ( (4 + 3)/2, (y + 5)/2 )<br/>
								1 + x = 7 ⟹ <strong>x = 6</strong><br/>
								8 = y + 5 ⟹ <strong>y = 3</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Trisection points divide the line in ratios <strong>1 : 2</strong> and <strong>2 : 1</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Parallelogram property: <strong>Mid-point of Diagonal 1 = Mid-point of Diagonal 2</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Centroid formula: <strong>( (x₁+x₂+x₃)/3, (y₁+y₂+y₃)/3 )</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/coordinate-geometry/section-formula" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Section Formula</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/coordinate-geometry/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">COORDINATE GEOMETRY</div>
